### Problem Statement
When utilizing watch expressions inside the VS Code debugger layout, evaluating an identifier that exists in both local function scope and outer global scopes simultaneously causes visual duplication or state collision. Developers are forced to manually inject runtime-specific scope paths to isolate namespace variables.

### Proposed Solution
Implement a native, configurable Debug Adapter Protocol (DAP) tracker proxy layer that hooks into incoming evaluate packets to cleanly target local scope evaluations first. 

### Working Prototype
I have built a functional open-source proof-of-concept extension implementing this feature via onWillReceiveMessage evaluation hooks.

