README (excerpt):

> # VS Code Watch Expression Deduplicator
>
> Eliminate scope clutter in your debugging workflow. This extension intercepts the Debug Adapter Protocol (DAP) to safely filter out redundant local and global variable tracking. It features an intuitive status bar toggle and scope isolation capabilities.

Key files / quick links:
- README: https://github.com/parseRcDw6942/my-work/blob/main/README.md
- Core extension source: https://github.com/parseRcDw6942/my-work/blob/main/src/src/extension.ts

Small code excerpt (src/src/extension.ts):

```typescript
import * as vscode from 'vscode';

let statusBarItem: vscode.StatusBarItem;
const variableHighlightType = vscode.window.createTextEditorDecorationType({
    backgroundColor: 'rgba(255, 235, 59, 0.3)', 
    border: '1px solid yellow',
    borderRadius: '2px'
});

export function activate(context: vscode.ExtensionContext) {
    // 1. Register the Toggle Command
    context.subscriptions.push(
        vscode.commands.registerCommand('watchDeduplicator.toggle', async () => {
            const config = vscode.workspace.getConfiguration('watchDeduplicator');
            const currentState = config.get<boolean>('enabled', true);
            await config.update('enabled', !currentState, vscode.ConfigurationTarget.Global);
            updateStatusBar(!currentState);
            vscode.window.showInformationMessage(`Watch Proxy is now ${!currentState ? 'ON' : 'OFF'}`);
        })
    );
```

Usage guide (short):
1. Install the extension from this repository (dev install) or from Marketplace once published.
2. Toggle the Watch Deduplicator via the status bar or the command palette (Watch Proxy).
3. Configure behavior in settings (example key: `watchDeduplicator.enabled`).

